{"kind":"finding","id":"F-logistics-route-038-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/RouteEndpointRootIdResolutionTests.cs","line":161,"method":"RouteBuilderStampsTheRootIdOntoTheOriginEndpoint_AndItRoundTrips","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Logistics/RouteNodeCodec.cs:SerializeEndpoint rootPartUId write; drop the key -> red","what_it_asserts":"a hand-built RouteEndpoint with RootPartUId=4242 serializes the rootPartUId key and deserializes back to 4242","why_weak":"the name and the FAILS IF comment claim the route BUILDER stamps the root id onto Route.Origin; no builder code runs, so a builder that stops stamping leaves this green and the resolver's first step goes dead exactly as the comment fears","proposed_action":"either rename to a codec round-trip test, or add a case that drives the route-creation path and asserts Route.Origin.RootPartUId","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-logistics-route-038-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/LogisticsCapacityContextTests.cs","line":79,"method":"FormatCapacityContext_InvariantCulture_NoCommaDecimal","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/UI/LogisticsDeliveryPresentation.cs:597 FormatCapacityContext; drop InvariantCulture from the F1 format calls -> red only under a comma-decimal culture","what_it_asserts":"the formatted capacity clause contains dot decimals and no comma decimals","why_weak":"no culture is installed for the test, so on a dot-decimal host the assertion holds even with the InvariantCulture pin removed; the suite convention elsewhere is to install de-DE to PROVE a site is invariant","proposed_action":"wrap the act in a de-DE CultureInfo scope (as the culture-pinning tests elsewhere do) so removing the pin reds on every host","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
